2.28.m:
Jamadagni said:
"I am never in any way an agent of buying and selling;
therefore, I cannot bear to give away the yielder of oblations straight out."

The minister said:
"Give this single cow in exchange for half the king's realm, or even the whole [of it], O brahmin;
that will be for your welfare."

The minister said:
"Give the cow to the king of your own free will, out of friendship;
otherwise, what will you do when she is carried off by force?"

2.37.m:
Kṛṣṇa said:
“Come, O fortunate Rāma, your excellent purpose is accomplished;
know it to be so through the power of the armor and of the hymn.
